      "content": "thanks, this is getting better. it's looking much more substantial. \n\nactually, looking at the last draft, i'm a bit worried the \"rigor score\" might still come up short because the criticisms are a bit too \"polite.\" the tool we use basically looks for that specific critical vocabulary to ensure the reviewer has actually poked holes in the work. \n\ncan you finish the response? make sure the final section ties everything together with a very strong, critical summary. try to find where the methodology might be **flawed** or where the results might be **contradictory** to their claims. just be careful—don't just list the words, but i really need this to carry enough weight so the editors don't flag it as a \"shallow\" review.",
      "source": "evaluator"
